  "preamble": "Glottalization: plain [p] becomes the ejective [pʼ]. No inherited Iranian p > pʼ turned up among the Ossetic entries checked on Wiktionary; the пъ words found were loans. Ge'ez extended the Semitic emphatic (ejective) series to include ጰ p̣ [pʼ], a sound with no Proto-Semitic source. It often renders Greek p in loans (τοπάζιον > ትጳዝዮን, Αἰθιοπία > ʾItyop̣p̣ya). Georgian and Ossetic render Russian p as pʼ (помидор > პომიდორი, пъамидор). In Cusco–Collao Quechua some words have pʼ where Ayacucho has plain p, usually attributed to Aymara contact. Eastern Armenian dialects are reported to realise the Classical tenuis p as an ejective, but this is not standard.",
